        "prerequisite_note": "No command-line knowledge is needed. Type into the switch settings; Check configuration applies the draft and tests it.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "A group on a shared switch",
            "text": "A VLAN keeps one group\u2019s broadcast messages separate from another group on the same switch. A workstation uses an access port, which puts its untagged messages into one VLAN."
          },
          {
            "title": "Carry the group between switches",
            "text": "A trunk carries several groups over one cable. A tag identifies the VLAN, except for the configured native VLAN, which travels untagged in this model. Both switches need the group active and allowed on the trunk."
          }
        ],
        "example_description": "Separate practice uses staff VLAN 30 and guest VLAN 40. Inspect the right switch\u2019s staff port. Load example settings if you want to see the repair, then apply and test.",
